  "reference_notes": "Inspected the Wildlife Trusts compound leaf photograph and RHS spring shoots on arching canes, then current small/medium/large pilots and all 36 variants. Added attached three-leaflet clusters, lowered curved cane ends, widened spread and reduced excess terminal density after the first pilot resembled a round shrub. Current open scrambling or dense mound variants span 0.80-1.65 m. Rubus fruticosus is treated as the bramble aggregate, not a claim to one microspecies. Tiny hooked prickles and leaf teeth are unresolved at 25 mm; no autumn fruit is generated. Accepted as a stylized spring bramble thicket source, pending user endorsement.",
